From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:27:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Build VideoPacketSender.cpp and VideoFEC.cpp with autotools

VoIPController references tgvoip::video::VideoPacketSender unconditionally,
but Makefile.am never lists video/VideoPacketSender.cpp or video/VideoFEC.cpp
(which VideoPacketSender uses), so an autotools build produces a libtgvoip
that leaves those symbols undefined. Linking it into a shared object
succeeds, and the failure only shows when that object is loaded:
the Telegram libpurple plugin refused to load with an undefined tgvoip
symbol.

Add both files to libtgvoip_la_SOURCES. The other build systems (gyp,
Xcode, MSVC) already compile them. Makefile.in is not touched here; it is
regenerated by autoreconf.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 Makefile.am | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index 0d1f1b5..6e308fd 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@ audio/Resampler.cpp \
 os/posix/NetworkSocketPosix.cpp \
 video/VideoSource.cpp \
 video/VideoRenderer.cpp \
+video/VideoPacketSender.cpp \
+video/VideoFEC.cpp \
 video/ScreamCongestionController.cpp \
 json11.cpp
 
